        "sentence": "30 years. U.S. custody began August 18, 1950, before sentencing on April 5, 1951. Released January 14, 1969 with credit for presentence custody and good time; the commonly quoted 17 years 9 months excludes presentence detention."
      },
      "rationale": "Second Circuit establishes August 18, 1950 U.S. arrest and uninterrupted pretrial custody because bail was not posted. April 5, 1951 sentencing is distinct. Sobell v. Reed (1971) independently establishes January 14, 1969 actual release, not merely the appeal date. Earlier seizure in Mexico is not included in this U.S. custody interval.",
